<div class="verify-only">
    <h5>Result</h5>
    <div class="worked-out">
        <p class="verdict" data-output="verdict" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="clock" data-output="clock">
            <strong data-result aria-live="polite"></strong>
            <span data-detail></span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h5>Checks</h5>
    <ol class="checks">
        <li data-output="check-decode">
            <strong data-result></strong>
            <div>Decode the signature <span data-detail></span></div>
        </li>
        <li data-output="check-key">
            <strong data-result></strong>
            <div>Read the public key <span data-detail></span></div>
        </li>
        <li data-output="check-signature">
            <strong data-result></strong>
            <div>Verify the signature <span data-detail></span></div>
        </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mismatch" data-output="mismatch" hidden>
        A signature either verifies or does not, so this cannot say which part differs. Compare the string with the
        one you signed. Check that the body is byte for byte what was signed, that <code>$1</code> is the domain the
        request was sent to, that the path was not re-encoded, and that the key is the right one.
    </p>

    <h5>Not Checked Here</h5>
    <ul class="limits">
        <li>That the key belongs to the instance in <code>Versia-Signed-By</code>.</li>
        <li>That a response came from the instance the request was sent to.</li>
        <li>That the signature has not been seen before.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<style>
    /* The answer, ahead of the steps that led to it. Two results, since a good signature on a
       stale message is still refused. */
    p.verdict {
        margin: 0;
    }

    .verdict,
    .clock [data-result] {
        display: block;
        font-size: var(--text-body);
        font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
        line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .clock [data-detail] {
        display: block;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .verdict[data-state="pass"],
    [data-state="pass"] > strong {
        color: var(--value);
    }

    .verdict[data-state="fail"],
    [data-state="fail"] > strong {
        color: var(--accent);
    }

    /* A stale timestamp is a problem with the message, not a cryptographic failure. */
    .clock[data-state="warn"] > strong {
        color: var(--warn);
    }

    .checks {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
    }

    .checks li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 4rem minmax(0, 1fr);
        margin: 0;
    }

    .checks li + li {
        margin-top: 0.15rem;
    }

    .checks [data-result] {
        font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    }

    .checks [data-detail] {
        display: block;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    p.mismatch {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    }

    .limits {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 1.25em;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .limits li + li {
        margin-top: 0.15rem;
    }
</style>
